<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Thriumph for Discipline Priest Healer Phase 3</h3>These new Emblems will drop from both raid sizes of <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a>, <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=2159/onyxias-lair">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Onyxia's Lair</span></a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4603/vault-of-archavon">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Vault of Archavon</span></a> as well as the new daily Heroic++ dungeons for a possible maximum of 90 per week. However, with T9 being outclassed by T8 for Discipline Priests, the items you can purchase with these mostly just end up being mediocre catch-up gear.<br/>
<br/>For a new character buying the T8 tokens might actually be the most worthwhile way to use this currency as you will keep using the pieces throughout the phase, but at this point simply getting into an <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> raid should be possible before collecting that many badges, which might allow you to pick up these items at no cost.<br/>
<br/>Next up there are three items that are all somewhat worse than their respective hardmode raid drops from the previous phase, but are good placeholders to fill those slots with as a fresh player.<br/>
<br/>As mentioned later in the guide, the only reason a player who is currently using T8 4p might want a T9 piece is to use it as their offpiece item but even in that regard the 245 pieces are slightly worse than certain offset pieces from the previous raid tier, with the shoulders and chest being the closest. <br/>
<br/>Outside of that, the high emblem cost and the fact you typically want to hold out until you have the trophies from T9 raids so you can opt for the higher item level version prevents them from being an effective way to catch up on gear, as you will replace them with the T8 set as soon as possible.<br/>
