<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="weapons">Weapons and Offhands for Discipline Priest Healer Phase 3</h2>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="main-and-two-handed-weapons-for-discipline-priest-healer-phase-3">Main and Two-Handed Weapons for Discipline Priest Healer Phase 3</h4>Despite Discipline Priests being the healer that benefits least from <a class="q5 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46017/valanyr-hammer-of-ancient-kings">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_99.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Val'anyr, Hammer of Ancient Kings</span></a>, its stats are obviously still on-par with the new weapons, so the small amount of value we get from the proc make it pull slightly ahead of them if you do have access to it.<br/>
<br/>As that will not be the case for the majority, the best alternatives are listed in the table below. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48519/relentless-gladiators-salvation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_111.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relentless Gladiator's Salvation</span></a> has the highest spellpower and some extra stamina but is quite hard to acquire for the average player. For that reason, the new ToGC mace should be the most realistic option in this slot, while still being a perfectly good weapon.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Weapon Enchants</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=60714/enchant-weapon-mighty-spellpower">
